From 2a324ae80ae54592fada04e783263d5e98224594 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Sergi=E3=83=BB=E3=82=BB=E3=83=AB=E3=82=B8?=
 <xerpi.g.12@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 10:15:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 43/52] kernel: share one wait loop between sync objects
 (#4307)

* ci: expect gxm_shader_patcher_memory to fail

Since 6fe288365 a NULL host allocation callback ends instead of hanging, so the test now fails
instead of timing out.

* ci: bump VitaAutotests

* kernel: keep a lightweight mutex owned after its count wraps

A recursive lightweight mutex's count can wrap negative, and a wrapped count counted as free, so
any thread's next lock took the mutex.
It now stays owned while it has an owner, and the owner's lock fails with
`SCE_KERNEL_ERROR_LW_MUTEX_LOCK_OVF` when it would leave the count below 0.

* kernel: share one wait loop between sync objects

wait_loop() replaces wait_on(). It runs the pending callbacks, tries the object's take, sleeps in
the queue, and starts over after a callback notify.

Object waits now get a copy of the timeout, written back when the call returns. Message pipes
still get the caller's.

* kernel: return NOTIFY_CALLBACK when a simple event takes its bits after callbacks

A simple event wait that got its bits right after its callbacks ran returned 0.
It now returns `NOTIFY_CALLBACK`, with the bits and user data written.

(cherry picked from commit 99ec7cad651cc0ad7597f906c70a933e8702be62)
